{
  "skill": "terraform-secure-iac",
  "notes": [
    "Five prompts should route to this skill and five are adjacent but out of scope, so both over-triggering and under-triggering are measurable.",
    "One out-of-scope probe is the case the skill's 'When NOT to use this' section names: a formatting-only change with no security-relevant content. Another belongs to terraform-testing.",
    "A probe is correct when the skill fired and was expected to, or did not fire and was not expected to."
  ],
  "prompts": [
    {
      "id": "tsi-t01",
      "expect": "trigger",
      "prompt": "Add an S3 backend block to this Terraform root so the team stops sharing state over Slack."
    },
    {
      "id": "tsi-t02",
      "expect": "trigger",
      "prompt": "The Terraform module takes the API token as a plain variable and echoes it in an output. Clean that up."
    },
    {
      "id": "tsi-t03",
      "expect": "trigger",
      "prompt": "Review the IAM role our Terraform pipeline assumes before we let it apply to production."
    },
    {
      "id": "tsi-t04",
      "expect": "trigger",
      "prompt": "Our Terraform modules point at a Git repository with no ref. Fix the module sources and the provider constraints."
    },
    {
      "id": "tsi-t05",
      "expect": "trigger",
      "prompt": "Write the Terraform for a KMS key and an RDS instance whose master password Terraform never sees."
    },
    {
      "id": "tsi-t06",
      "expect": "no-trigger",
      "prompt": "Run terraform fmt over the repository and fix the indentation in the README's HCL examples."
    },
    {
      "id": "tsi-t07",
      "expect": "no-trigger",
      "prompt": "Add a terraform test file that checks the module's subnet_count variable rejects zero."
    },
    {
      "id": "tsi-t08",
      "expect": "no-trigger",
      "prompt": "Convert this CloudFormation template's parameters section to use SSM parameter types."
    },
    {
      "id": "tsi-t09",
      "expect": "no-trigger",
      "prompt": "Our Ansible role writes AWS credentials into ~/.aws/credentials on the build host. Move them to an instance profile."
    },
    {
      "id": "tsi-t10",
      "expect": "no-trigger",
      "prompt": "Explain the difference between terraform plan and terraform apply -refresh-only. No code changes needed."
    }
  ]
}
skills/bash/bash-testing/SKILL.md:3:description: Adds or updates bats-core, shunit2, or plain-script test coverage for a Bash change by first discovering the repository's existing test layout and conventions, matching them rather than imposing a new framework, deciding whether the change requires a test at all, making a script testable by separating logic into functions from the entry point, and running the suite in a bounded verify loop. Use when a shell script's behavior changes and that change should be locked in, including fixing a bug so it cannot regress, pinning an exit code or output that is currently wrong, adding behavior, or covering input validation, cleanup, privilege, or destructive paths, and when deciding where a new shell test belongs in an unfamiliar repository. Not for test work in other languages, and not for documenting, explaining, or tuning CI for a script whose behavior is unchanged.
skills/bash/bash-secure-scripting/SKILL.md:3:description: Authors, reviews, and hardens Bash scripts for the stability and security properties a linter cannot verify on its own, including strict-mode semantics and the cases errexit ignores, cleanup and locking on every exit path, injection-safe handling of untrusted input and filenames, PATH and environment control, temporary files and permissions, and credential handling, verified with shellcheck, bash -n, and the repository's formatter in a bounded loop. Use when creating or editing a shell script, a sourced shell library, or shell embedded in CI `run:` steps, container entrypoints, systemd units, cron jobs, or git hooks, and when reviewing quoting, eval, set -euo pipefail, traps, temporary files, privilege or sudo use, or secrets in shell code. Not for workflow steps that only call an action, which belong to github-actions-security.
